### Rule 1: ALWAYS test what you create
- After creating or modifying ANY file, you MUST run/test it to verify it works

### Rule 2: ALWAYS output the full path when done
- Format: FULL PATH: C:/path/to/file

### Rule 3: NEVER create generic garbage
- Always create REAL, WORKING code with proper error handling

### Rule 4: ALWAYS show real-time progress
- Show what you're doing at each step

### Rule 5: PowerShell 5 compatibility
- All scripts MUST work in PowerShell 5.1
- Avoid PS6+ features like pipe-pipe, question-question, AsHashtable
- Use try/catch blocks instead of single-pipe error handling
- This host is Windows. Run PowerShell commands directly in the shell tool.
- NEVER wrap PowerShell with bash, /usr/bin/bash, sh, wsl, or powershell -Command.
- Use semicolons instead of &&. Preserve PowerShell variables such as `$_` literally.

### Rule 6: NEVER STOP until the task is achieved
- Never stop working before the user's request is fully and verifiably achieved, no matter how complex or how long it takes.
- Do not stop after partial work. Do not stop to ask "should I continue?" - just continue.
- Keep looping: plan -> execute -> test -> fix -> verify -> continue until done.
- If something fails, diagnose it, fix it, and retry with a different approach. Never report failure as the outcome while a path forward exists.
- Only stop when the request is fully implemented AND verified working, or when the user manually stops you.
"@
        $defaultInstructions | Set-Content -LiteralPath $instructionsPath -Encoding UTF8
        Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=instructions-created path=$instructionsPath"
    }

    if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $buildPromptPath -PathType Leaf)) {
        $buildPromptDir = Split-Path -Parent $buildPromptPath
        if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $buildPromptDir -PathType Container)) {
            New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $buildPromptDir | Out-Null
        }
        $defaultBuildPrompt = @'
# Build Agent Rules

You are the build agent. You turn requests into real, working, verified code. You FINISH what you start.

## THE #1 RULE - NEVER STOP UNTIL THE GOAL IS ACHIEVED

You must NEVER stop working before the user's request is fully and verifiably achieved - no matter how
complex, how long it takes, or how many obstacles appear. This is non-negotiable and overrides everything
else except an explicit manual stop by the user (Ctrl+C / Esc / "stop").

- Do not stop after a partial implementation. Do not stop after "a good start". Do not stop to ask
  "should I continue?" - JUST CONTINUE.
- Keep working in a loop: plan -> execute -> test -> fix -> verify -> continue, until the task is done.
- If a step fails or an error appears, do NOT stop and report the failure as the outcome. Diagnose it,
  fix it, and retry. Try alternative approaches until one works.
- If you are uncertain, investigate (read files, search, web fetch, run commands) until you are certain.
- Only stop when BOTH are true: (1) the user's request is fully implemented, and (2) you have verified
  it actually works by running/testing it. If either is false, keep going.
- Break large tasks into steps and track them with the todo tool. Work through the list to completion
  without being asked.
- If a truly external blocker exists (e.g., a service is down, credentials missing), do everything you
  can to work around it first. Only if there is literally no path forward do you report the blocker -
  and say exactly what is blocking and what unblocks it.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. ALWAYS test what you create: after creating or modifying ANY file, run or test it to prove it works.
   If it doesn't work, fix it - never leave broken code behind.
2. ALWAYS report the full path of every file you create or modify. Format: FULL PATH: C:/path/to/file
3. NEVER create generic garbage: produce real, complete, working code with proper error handling.
4. ALWAYS show real-time progress: state what you are doing at each step before doing it.
5. PowerShell 5 compatibility: on Windows, scripts MUST work in Windows PowerShell 5.1 - no ??, no &&,
   no AsHashtable; use try/catch blocks. Run PowerShell directly; never nest it inside bash, sh, WSL,
   or powershell -Command because nested shells corrupt `$_` and quoting. Use semicolons instead of &&.
6. Never leave broken or half-finished work. If something cannot be completed, say exactly what is
   blocking it - after exhausting every workaround.

Use any tool you need to verify your work. When the task is done, summarize exactly what changed and
how it was verified.
'@
        $defaultBuildPrompt | Set-Content -LiteralPath $buildPromptPath -Encoding UTF8
        Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=build-prompt-created path=$buildPromptPath"
    }

    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # LAUNCH OPENCODE - IMMEDIATELY (auto-heals if missing)
    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    function Resolve-NviocOpenCode {
        # The platform binary lives directly in opencode-ai\bin AND (as a
        # hard link) in the optional opencode-windows-x64 package. PowerShell
        # 5.1 cannot reliably launch the Bun executable directly, so prefer
        # npm's command shim and validate the native executable only as a
        # fallback.
        $candidates = @(
            (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'OpenCodeStable\opencode.cmd'),
            (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'npm-global\opencode.cmd'),
            (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'npm-global\node_modules\opencode-ai\bin\opencode.exe'),
            (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'npm-global\node_modules\opencode-ai\node_modules\opencode-windows-x64\bin\opencode.exe'),
            (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'npm-global\node_modules\opencode-ai\node_modules\opencode-windows-x64-baseline\bin\opencode.exe'),
            (Join-Path $env:APPDATA 'npm\node_modules\opencode-ai\bin\opencode.exe')
        )
        foreach ($candidate in $candidates) {
            if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $candidate -PathType Leaf) { return $candidate }
        }
        foreach ($shim in @('opencode.cmd', 'opencode')) {
            $cmd = Get-Command $shim -CommandType Application -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
            if ($cmd -and $cmd.Source) { return $cmd.Source }
        }
        return $null
    }

    function Test-NviocOpenCodeWorks {
        param([string]$Path)
        $receiptPath = "$Path.verified.json"
        try {
            if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $receiptPath -PathType Leaf) {
                $receipt = Get-Content -LiteralPath $receiptPath -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
                $file = Get-Item -LiteralPath $Path
                if ([long]$receipt.length -eq $file.Length -and
                    [long]$receipt.lastWriteTimeUtcTicks -eq $file.LastWriteTimeUtc.Ticks -and
                    [string]$receipt.identity -eq 'opencode models') {
                    return $true
                }
            }
        } catch { }

        # Bun itself also returns a semantic version, so verify an OpenCode-only
        # command signature before trusting a native executable or shim.
        try {
            $version = (& $Path '--version' 2>$null) -join " "
            if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0 -or $version -notmatch '^\s*\d+\.\d+\.\d+\s*$') { return $false }
            $helpCommand = '"{0}" models --help 2>&1' -f $Path
            $help = ((& $env:ComSpec /d /s /c $helpCommand) -join "`n") -replace "`e\[[0-9;]*m", ''
            if ($help -match '(?m)^\s*opencode\s+models\b') {
                try {
                    $file = Get-Item -LiteralPath $Path
                    [pscustomobject]@{
                        length = $file.Length
                        lastWriteTimeUtcTicks = $file.LastWriteTimeUtc.Ticks
                        version = $version.Trim()
                        identity = 'opencode models'
                    } | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath $receiptPath -Encoding UTF8
                } catch { }
                return $true
            }
        } catch { }
        return $false
    }

    $openCodePath = Resolve-NviocOpenCode
    if ($openCodePath -and -not (Test-NviocOpenCodeWorks -Path $openCodePath)) {
        Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=invalid-binary path=$openCodePath"
        $openCodePath = $null
    }
    if (-not $openCodePath) {
        # Never fail with 'not installed': run the permanent installer on the
        # spot and re-resolve (same auto-bootstrap as the oc launcher).
        Write-Host 'OC_PROGRESS stage=not-installed-auto-bootstrap'
        $installer = 'F:\study\Platforms\windows\functions\getoc2.ps1'
        if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $installer -PathType Leaf) {
            & $installer
            if (-not $?) {
                throw "nvioc: opencode auto-install failed: $installer"
            }
        } else {
            throw "nvioc: opencode auto-install script is missing: $installer"
        }
        $openCodePath = Resolve-NviocOpenCode
        Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=auto-installed path=$openCodePath"
        if ($openCodePath -and -not (Test-NviocOpenCodeWorks -Path $openCodePath)) {
            throw "nvioc: OpenCode bootstrap returned an unusable command: $openCodePath"
        }
    }
    if (-not $openCodePath) {
        throw 'nvioc: opencode could not be installed. Check your network / npm, then run getoc2 manually.'
    }

    Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=launching model=$finalModelArg label=$finalLabel"
    # OpenCode snapshots contend on one internal Git worktree when many nvi
    # sessions start together. Disable only that local bookkeeping layer for
    # this launch; model reasoning, tools, context, and user files are unchanged.
    $previousConfigContent = $env:OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT
    try {
        $runtimeConfig = [ordered]@{}
        if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($previousConfigContent)) {
            try {
                $existingRuntimeConfig = $previousConfigContent | ConvertFrom-Json
                foreach ($property in $existingRuntimeConfig.PSObject.Properties) {
                    $runtimeConfig[$property.Name] = $property.Value
                }
            } catch {
                Write-Host 'OC_PROGRESS stage=config-content-invalid using=nvi-safe-runtime'
            }
        }
        $runtimeConfig['snapshot'] = $false
        $runtimeAgents = [ordered]@{}
        if ($runtimeConfig.Contains('agent') -and $null -ne $runtimeConfig['agent']) {
            foreach ($property in $runtimeConfig['agent'].PSObject.Properties) {
                $runtimeAgents[$property.Name] = $property.Value
            }
        }
        $runtimeTitleAgent = [ordered]@{}
        if ($runtimeAgents.Contains('title') -and $null -ne $runtimeAgents['title']) {
            foreach ($property in $runtimeAgents['title'].PSObject.Properties) {
                $runtimeTitleAgent[$property.Name] = $property.Value
            }
        }
        $runtimeTitleAgent['disable'] = $true
        $runtimeAgents['title'] = $runtimeTitleAgent
        $runtimeConfig['agent'] = $runtimeAgents
        # OpenCode 1.18 still invokes its hidden title worker even when that
        # agent is disabled. Keep the cosmetic request off the selected model
        # and route it through the verified low-latency 9B endpoint instead.
        $runtimeConfig['small_model'] = 'nvidia-nim/nvidia/nvidia-nemotron-nano-9b-v2'
        $env:OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT = $runtimeConfig | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 20 -Compress

        # OpenCode 1.18 opens the same SQLite database independently in every
        # local TUI/run process. Thirty simultaneous clients can therefore fail
        # with "database is locked" before the selected model is contacted.
        # Keep one localhost-only OpenCode backend as the sole database owner;
        # every nvi client attaches to it and retains the shared session history.
        $sharedServerPort = 4097
        $sharedServerUrl = "http://127.0.0.1:$sharedServerPort"
        $sharedServerMutexName = 'Local\NviOpenCodeSharedServer4097'
        $sharedServerOutLog = Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'OpenCodeStable\shared-server.out.log'
        $sharedServerErrLog = Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'OpenCodeStable\shared-server.err.log'

        function Resolve-NviocServerExecutable {
            $serverCandidates = @(
                (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'OpenCodeStable\opencode.exe'),
                (Join-Path (Split-Path -Parent $openCodePath) 'opencode.exe'),
                (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'npm-global\node_modules\opencode-ai\bin\opencode.exe'),
                (Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'npm-global\node_modules\opencode-ai\node_modules\opencode-windows-x64\bin\opencode.exe')
            )
            foreach ($candidate in $serverCandidates) {
                if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $candidate -PathType Leaf) {
                    return [IO.Path]::GetFullPath($candidate)
                }
            }
            return $null
        }

        function Get-NviocListenerProcessIds {
            param([int]$Port)
            $listenerIds = @()
            try {
                foreach ($connection in @(Get-NetTCPConnection -State Listen -LocalPort $Port -ErrorAction Stop)) {
                    if ([int]$connection.OwningProcess -gt 0) {
                        $listenerIds += [int]$connection.OwningProcess
                    }
                }
            } catch {
                $netstatPath = Join-Path $env:SystemRoot 'System32\netstat.exe'
                if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $netstatPath -PathType Leaf) {
                    foreach ($line in @(& $netstatPath -ano -p tcp 2>$null)) {
                        if ($line -match ('^\s*TCP\s+\S+:' + [regex]::Escape([string]$Port) + '\s+\S+\s+LISTENING\s+(\d+)\s*$')) {
                            $listenerIds += [int]$matches[1]
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            return @($listenerIds | Select-Object -Unique)
        }

        function Test-NviocSharedServerIdentity {
            param(
                [int]$Port,
                [string]$ServerExecutable
            )
            $listenerIds = @(Get-NviocListenerProcessIds -Port $Port)
            if ($listenerIds.Count -ne 1) { return $false }
            try {
                $listener = Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter "ProcessId=$($listenerIds[0])" -ErrorAction Stop
                if (-not $listener -or $listener.Name -ne 'opencode.exe') { return $false }
                $commandLine = [string]$listener.CommandLine
                if ($commandLine -notmatch '(?i)\bserve\b' -or
                    $commandLine -notmatch ('(?i)--port\s+' + [regex]::Escape([string]$Port) + '(?:\s|$)')) {
                    return $false
                }
                $expectedPath = [IO.Path]::GetFullPath($ServerExecutable)
                if ($listener.ExecutablePath) {
                    return [string]::Equals(
                        [IO.Path]::GetFullPath([string]$listener.ExecutablePath),
                        $expectedPath,
                        [StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase
                    )
                }
                return $commandLine.IndexOf($expectedPath, [StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase) -ge 0
            } catch {
                return $false
            }
        }

        function Test-NviocSharedServer {
            param(
                [string]$Url,
                [int]$Port,
                [string]$ServerExecutable,
                [string]$ExpectedVersion
            )
            try {
                $health = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "$Url/global/health" -Method Get -TimeoutSec 2 -ErrorAction Stop
                if (-not $health.healthy -or [string]$health.version -ne $ExpectedVersion) {
                    return $false
                }
                return Test-NviocSharedServerIdentity -Port $Port -ServerExecutable $ServerExecutable
            } catch {
                return $false
            }
        }

        function Ensure-NviocSharedServer {
            param(
                [string]$Url,
                [int]$Port,
                [string]$ServerExecutable,
                [string]$ExpectedVersion
            )
            if (Test-NviocSharedServer -Url $Url -Port $Port -ServerExecutable $ServerExecutable -ExpectedVersion $ExpectedVersion) {
                Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-server-ready port=$Port version=$ExpectedVersion"
                return
            }

            $serverMutex = New-Object Threading.Mutex($false, $sharedServerMutexName)
            $serverLockTaken = $false
            try {
                try {
                    $serverLockTaken = $serverMutex.WaitOne(30000)
                } catch [Threading.AbandonedMutexException] {
                    $serverLockTaken = $true
                }
                if (-not $serverLockTaken) {
                    throw "nvioc: timed out waiting for shared OpenCode server startup on port $Port."
                }
                if (Test-NviocSharedServer -Url $Url -Port $Port -ServerExecutable $ServerExecutable -ExpectedVersion $ExpectedVersion) {
                    Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-server-ready port=$Port version=$ExpectedVersion"
                    return
                }

                $listeners = @(Get-NviocListenerProcessIds -Port $Port)
                if ($listeners.Count -gt 0) {
                    throw "nvioc: port $Port is owned by an unverified process (PID $($listeners -join ',')). Refusing to replace it."
                }

                Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-server-starting port=$Port"
                $serverProcess = Start-Process -FilePath $ServerExecutable -ArgumentList @(
                    'serve',
                    '--hostname', '127.0.0.1',
                    '--port', [string]$Port,
                    '--print-logs',
                    '--log-level', 'WARN'
                ) -WindowStyle Hidden -RedirectStandardOutput $sharedServerOutLog `
                    -RedirectStandardError $sharedServerErrLog -PassThru -ErrorAction Stop

                $started = $false
                for ($attempt = 1; $attempt -le 200; $attempt++) {
                    if (Test-NviocSharedServer -Url $Url -Port $Port -ServerExecutable $ServerExecutable -ExpectedVersion $ExpectedVersion) {
                        $started = $true
                        break
                    }
                    if ($serverProcess.HasExited) { break }
                    if (($attempt % 20) -eq 0) {
                        Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-server-wait port=$Port elapsed_ms=$($attempt * 100)"
                    }
                    Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 100
                }
                if (-not $started) {
                    $detail = ''
                    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $sharedServerErrLog -PathType Leaf) {
                        $detail = ((Get-Content -LiteralPath $sharedServerErrLog -Tail 8) -join ' ')
                    }
                    if (-not $serverProcess.HasExited) {
                        Stop-Process -Id $serverProcess.Id -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
                    }
                    throw "nvioc: shared OpenCode server failed to become healthy. $detail"
                }
                Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-server-started port=$Port pid=$($serverProcess.Id) version=$ExpectedVersion"
                $serverProcess.Dispose()
            } finally {
                if ($serverLockTaken) {
                    [void]$serverMutex.ReleaseMutex()
                }
                $serverMutex.Dispose()
            }
        }

        function Get-NviocDirectoryHeaders {
            param([string]$Directory)
            return @{ 'x-opencode-directory' = $Directory }
        }

        function New-NviocSharedSession {
            param(
                [string]$Url,
                [string]$Directory,
                [string]$Model,
                [string]$Label
            )
            $providerModel = $Model -replace '^nvidia-nim/', ''
            $payload = [ordered]@{
                title = "NVI | $Label"
                agent = 'build'
                model = [ordered]@{
                    providerID = 'nvidia-nim'
                    id = $providerModel
                    variant = 'default'
                }
            } | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 8 -Compress
            $headers = Get-NviocDirectoryHeaders -Directory $Directory
            $lastError = $null
            for ($attempt = 1; $attempt -le 3; $attempt++) {
                try {
                    $session = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "$Url/session" -Method Post -Headers $headers `
                        -ContentType 'application/json' -Body $payload -TimeoutSec 15 -ErrorAction Stop
                    if ($session.id -and
                        [string]$session.model.providerID -eq 'nvidia-nim' -and
                        [string]$session.model.id -eq $providerModel) {
                        return $session
                    }
                    $lastError = 'server returned a session without the requested model'
                } catch {
                    $lastError = $_.Exception.Message
                }
                Start-Sleep -Milliseconds (100 * $attempt)
            }
            throw "nvioc: could not create the model-pinned shared session: $lastError"
        }

        function Invoke-NviocSharedRun {
            param(
                [string]$Path,
                [string]$Url,
                [string]$Directory,
                [string]$Model,
                [string]$Label,
                [string[]]$RunArguments
            )

            $jsonRequested = $false
            $showThinking = $false
            $hasDirectory = $false
            $requestedSessionId = $null
            $continueRequested = $false
            $normalized = @()
            for ($index = 0; $index -lt $RunArguments.Count; $index++) {
                $argument = [string]$RunArguments[$index]
                if ($argument -eq '--format') {
                    if ($index + 1 -lt $RunArguments.Count) {
                        $jsonRequested = [string]$RunArguments[$index + 1] -eq 'json'
                        $index++
                    }
                    continue
                }
                if ($argument -match '^--format=(.+)$') {
                    $jsonRequested = $matches[1] -eq 'json'
                    continue
                }
                if ($argument -eq '-s' -or $argument -eq '--session') {
                    if ($index + 1 -lt $RunArguments.Count) {
                        $requestedSessionId = [string]$RunArguments[$index + 1]
                    }
                } elseif ($argument -match '^--session=(.+)$') {
                    $requestedSessionId = $matches[1]
                } elseif ($argument -eq '-c' -or $argument -eq '--continue') {
                    $continueRequested = $true
                }
                if ($argument -eq '--thinking') { $showThinking = $true }
                if ($argument -eq '--dir' -or $argument -match '^--dir=') { $hasDirectory = $true }
                if ($argument -eq '--attach') {
                    if ($index + 1 -lt $RunArguments.Count) { $index++ }
                    continue
                }
                if ($argument -match '^--attach=') { continue }
                $normalized += $argument
            }

            $clientArguments = @('run', '--attach', $Url, '-m', $Model, '--format', 'json')
            $sessionId = $requestedSessionId
            if (-not $sessionId -and -not $continueRequested) {
                # Attached run can submit successfully and then exit before its
                # event stream prints the generated session ID. Create the
                # model-pinned session first so response recovery never depends
                # on that lossy client event.
                $preparedSession = New-NviocSharedSession -Url $Url -Directory $Directory `
                    -Model $Model -Label $Label
                $sessionId = [string]$preparedSession.id
                $clientArguments += @('--session', $sessionId)
                Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-run-session-created session=$sessionId model=$Model"
            }
            if (-not $hasDirectory) {
                $clientArguments += @('--dir', $Directory)
            }
            $clientArguments += $normalized

            $capturedLines = New-Object 'Collections.Generic.List[string]'
            $seenPartIds = @{}
            & $Path @clientArguments 2>&1 | ForEach-Object {
                $line = [string]$_
                [void]$capturedLines.Add($line)
                $event = $null
                if ($line.TrimStart().StartsWith('{')) {
                    try { $event = $line | ConvertFrom-Json } catch { }
                }
                if ($event) {
                    if ($event.sessionID) { $sessionId = [string]$event.sessionID }
                    if ($event.part -and $event.part.id) { $seenPartIds[[string]$event.part.id] = $true }
                    if ($jsonRequested) {
                        Write-Output $line
                    } elseif ($event.type -eq 'step_start') {
                        Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-run-active session=$sessionId"
                    }
                } else {
                    Write-Output $line
                }
            }
            $nativeExitCode = [int]$LASTEXITCODE
            $resultCode = $nativeExitCode

            if ($sessionId) {
                $messages = $null
                $headers = Get-NviocDirectoryHeaders -Directory $Directory
                $lastReadError = $null
                $assistant = @()
                $assistantComplete = $false
                $requestObserved = $false
                $responseDeadline = [DateTime]::UtcNow.AddHours(2)
                $submissionDeadline = [DateTime]::UtcNow.AddSeconds(30)
                $nextProgress = [DateTime]::UtcNow.AddSeconds(2)
                $waitStopwatch = [Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()
                while ([DateTime]::UtcNow -lt $responseDeadline) {
                    try {
                        $messages = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "$Url/session/$sessionId/message" -Method Get `
                            -Headers $headers -TimeoutSec 15 -ErrorAction Stop
                        $lastReadError = $null
                        $requestObserved = @($messages | Where-Object { $_.info.role -eq 'user' }).Count -gt 0
                        $assistant = @($messages | Where-Object { $_.info.role -eq 'assistant' } |
                            Sort-Object { [int64]$_.info.time.created } | Select-Object -Last 1)
                        if ($assistant.Count -eq 1 -and
                            ($assistant[0].info.time.completed -or $assistant[0].info.error)) {
                            $assistantComplete = $true
                            break
                        }
                    } catch {
                        $lastReadError = $_.Exception.Message
                    }
                    if (-not $requestObserved -and [DateTime]::UtcNow -ge $submissionDeadline) {
                        break
                    }
                    if ([DateTime]::UtcNow -ge $nextProgress) {
                        $state = if ($requestObserved) { 'running' } else { 'submitting' }
                        Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-run-wait session=$sessionId state=$state elapsed_ms=$($waitStopwatch.ElapsedMilliseconds)"
                        $nextProgress = [DateTime]::UtcNow.AddSeconds(5)
                    }
                    Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200
                }
                $waitStopwatch.Stop()

                if ($assistantComplete) {
                    foreach ($part in @($assistant[0].parts)) {
                        if ($part.id -and $seenPartIds.ContainsKey([string]$part.id)) { continue }
                        $eventType = $null
                        if ($part.type -eq 'step-start') { $eventType = 'step_start' }
                        elseif ($part.type -eq 'step-finish') { $eventType = 'step_finish' }
                        elseif ($part.type -eq 'text') { $eventType = 'text' }
                        elseif ($part.type -eq 'reasoning') { $eventType = 'reasoning' }
                        elseif ($part.type -eq 'tool') { $eventType = 'tool_use' }
                        if (-not $eventType) { continue }

                        if ($jsonRequested) {
                            [ordered]@{
                                type = $eventType
                                timestamp = [DateTimeOffset]::UtcNow.ToUnixTimeMilliseconds()
                                sessionID = $sessionId
                                part = $part
                            } | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 30 -Compress | Write-Output
                        } elseif ($part.type -eq 'text' -and -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace([string]$part.text)) {
                            Write-Output ([string]$part.text).Trim()
                        } elseif ($part.type -eq 'reasoning' -and $showThinking -and -not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace([string]$part.text)) {
                            Write-Output ("Thinking: " + ([string]$part.text).Trim())
                        } elseif ($part.type -eq 'tool') {
                            Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=tool name=$($part.tool) status=$($part.state.status)"
                        }
                    }
                    if ($assistant[0].info.error) {
                        $errorDetail = $assistant[0].info.error | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 12 -Compress
                        throw "nvioc: shared run failed in session ${sessionId}: $errorDetail"
                    }
                } else {
                    $reason = if (-not $requestObserved) {
                        'the attached client did not submit a user message within 30 seconds'
                    } elseif ($lastReadError) {
                        "the assistant response could not be read: $lastReadError"
                    } else {
                        'the assistant response did not complete before the two-hour upstream deadline'
                    }
                    throw "nvioc: shared run session $sessionId failed because $reason."
                }
            } else {
                throw 'nvioc: attached continuation returned no session identifier.'
            }

            if ($resultCode -ne 0) {
                throw "nvioc: attached OpenCode client exited with code $resultCode."
            }
            $global:LASTEXITCODE = 0
        }

        $serverExecutable = Resolve-NviocServerExecutable
        if (-not $serverExecutable) {
            throw 'nvioc: the native OpenCode server executable is missing.'
        }
        $openCodeVersion = ((& $openCodePath '--version' 2>$null) -join '').Trim()
        if ($openCodeVersion -notmatch '^\d+\.\d+\.\d+$') {
            throw "nvioc: could not verify the OpenCode version at $openCodePath."
        }

        $firstArgument = if ($Args.Count -gt 0) { [string]$Args[0] } else { '' }
        $usesSharedServer = $Args.Count -eq 0 -or $firstArgument -eq 'run'
        if ($usesSharedServer) {
            Ensure-NviocSharedServer -Url $sharedServerUrl -Port $sharedServerPort `
                -ServerExecutable $serverExecutable -ExpectedVersion $openCodeVersion

            # The server deliberately has no global model. Pin the model in both
            # the client runtime and the individual session so 30 attached TUIs
            # can use 30 different models simultaneously.
            $runtimeConfig['model'] = $finalModelArg
            $env:OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT = $runtimeConfig | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 20 -Compress
            $currentDirectory = (Get-Location).ProviderPath

            if ($firstArgument -eq 'run') {
                $runArguments = @()
                if ($Args.Count -gt 1) { $runArguments = @($Args[1..($Args.Count - 1)]) }
                Invoke-NviocSharedRun -Path $serverExecutable -Url $sharedServerUrl `
                    -Directory $currentDirectory -Model $finalModelArg -Label $finalLabel `
                    -RunArguments $runArguments
            } else {
                $session = New-NviocSharedSession -Url $sharedServerUrl -Directory $currentDirectory `
                    -Model $finalModelArg -Label $finalLabel
                Write-Host "OC_PROGRESS stage=shared-session-ready session=$($session.id) model=$finalModelArg"
                & $serverExecutable 'attach' $sharedServerUrl '--mini' '--session' ([string]$session.id) `
                    '--dir' $currentDirectory
            }
        } else {
            # Metadata/debug commands do not open the session database and remain
            # direct, preserving the exact OpenCode CLI surface.
            & $openCodePath '-m' $finalModelArg @Args
        }
    } finally {
        if ($null -eq $previousConfigContent) {
            Remove-Item Env:OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
        } else {
            $env:OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT = $previousConfigContent
        }
    }
}

if ($MyInvocation.InvocationName -ne '.') {
    # Switches must be re-bound as real tokens: the profile module forwards
    # command-line args as a string ARRAY, and array-splatting '-Check' as a
    # positional string never binds the [switch]$Check parameter. Detect it
    # here and invoke with a literal switch token so -Check actually works.
    $__checkSwitch = $false
    $__passArgs = @()
    foreach ($__a in $args) {
        if ($__a -eq '-Check' -or $__a -eq '-check') {
            $__checkSwitch = $true
        } else {
            $__passArgs += $__a
        }
    }
    if ($__checkSwitch) {
        & 'nvioc' -Check @__passArgs
    } else {
        & 'nvioc' @__passArgs
    }
}
